  "portal_publication_date": "2012-11-07T17:01:55Z",
  "portal_product_names": ["JBoss Enterprise Web Server"],
  "abstract": "JBoss Enterprise Web Server (JBEWS) is a fully integrated and certified set of components for hosting Java web applications. It is comprised of the Apache HTTP Server, the Apache Tomcat Servlet container, Apache Tomcat Connector (mod_jk), JBoss HTTP Connector (mod_cluster), Hibernate, and the Tomcat Native library.\n\nThis enhancement update provides JBEWS 2.0 with improved capabilities on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 5. It aligns JBEWS with JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 6, improves integration with Red Hat Enterprise Linux, and enhances JBEWS with a subset of the frameworks of JBoss Web Framework 2.0. For detailed component and installation information refer to the Release Notes link in the References section of this advisory. (BZ#813395)\n\nNote: Do not install JBEWS 2 on a host which has JBEWS 1 installed.\n\nAll users who want to use JBoss Enterprise Web Server 2 are advised to upgrade to these updated JBEWS packages.",
